    {
      "id": "at-glance",
      "title": "At a glance",
      "body": "For travelers, Anh/chị nói tiếng Anh không? is the phrase to keep ready for \"Do you speak English\" in moments when Vietnamese stops making sense. This is for when you need to know whether English is an option. Switch the conversation toward English when Vietnamese stops working. It works best when you focus on asking for one clear help action before adding more words. The forms below help you choose the version that fits the person, setting, or level of politeness.",
      "presentation": "plain-text"
    },
    {
      "id": "breakdown",
      "title": "Break it down",
      "body": "This pattern asks for a yes-or-no answer. Keep the main need together so the question feels natural.",
