      "id": "why-it-matters",
      "title": "Why it matters",
      "body": "These phrases keep the interaction cooperative when repeating the same words is not helping. For \"Do you speak English\", Anh/chị nói tiếng Anh không? helps by asking for one clear help action before adding more words. If the first reply is still unclear, move to showing, writing, or pointing.",
      "presentation": "plain-text"
    },
    {
      "id": "traveler-insight",
      "title": "Traveler insight",
      "body": "In When You Don't Understand, the reply often comes as a slower repeat, a pointed explanation, or a switch to writing. Say Anh/chị nói tiếng Anh không? once, pause, and watch for the reply before adding another sentence. If speech still does not land, move to writing, pointing, or showing the exact word on your phone.",
